rypto Accounting is a SaaS platform that turns crypto-asset transactions into usable accounting: journal entries, the French FEC file, a full audit trail and tax reporting data.

It is built by chartered accountants for everyone who has to handle these transactions with the same rigour as any other flow:
- accounting firms and statutory auditors;
- companies that hold or receive crypto-assets;
- crypto-asset service providers (CASPs);
- individual investors, for capital gains and the French tax return.

In practice, Crypto Accounting:
- imports transactions from exchanges, wallets and CSV files, including uncommon formats;
- categorises operations (buys, sells, swaps, staking, airdrops and more);
- computes gains under the applicable method (weighted average cost or FIFO);
- handles the bank flows linked to crypto operations;
- generates journal entries and an auditable FEC, with control files to check every calculation;
- prepares, for companies, the information needed for the notes to the accounts and the management representation letter;
- exports to accounting software, including Pennylane.

The product follows French rules: ANC accounting standards for digital assets and French corporate and personal tax law. Versions for other European countries are in preparation.

Create your account at www.cryptoaccounting.fr or contact us for a demo.

